<% layout('./layout') %>
<article class="panel prose legal">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="muted">noticely/deps keeps as little as it can, for as short as it can. This page lists everything that is stored, why, and for how long.</p>

  <h2>Reports</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt>What is stored</dt><dd>Only the dependency names, version ranges and resolved versions from your file, and the resulting report. Never the whole file, scripts or other fields.</dd>
    <dt>Who can see it</dt><dd>Anyone with the report link, which contains a long random id. Package names are sent to the public npm registry, OSV.dev and deps.dev to look them up.</dd>
    <dt>How long</dt><dd>Deleted automatically after 30 days.</dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>Email lists</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt>What is stored</dt><dd>Your email address and the list you joined (PDF report or check packs).</dd>
    <dt>Confirmation</dt><dd>Unconfirmed addresses are deleted after 7 days. Once you confirm, the address is used only for that one announcement.</dd>
    <dt>Unsubscribing</dt><dd>Every email has an unsubscribe link. Unsubscribed addresses are deleted after 30 days.</dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>Contact form</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt>What is stored</dt><dd>Your name, email, optional company and message, used only to reply to you.</dd>
    <dt>How long</dt><dd>Up to 180 days.</dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>Abuse protection</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt>IP address</dt><dd>Stored only as a keyed hash to enforce the daily check limit, and deleted after 48 hours.</dd>
    <dt>Bot check</dt><dd>Cloudflare Turnstile runs on the forms to block bots. See Cloudflare's <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Turnstile privacy addendum</a>.</dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>Your data, your call</h2>
  <p>To ask what is stored about you or to have it deleted earlier, send a <a href="/contact?topic=privacy">privacy request</a>. It is answered within 30 days, usually much sooner.</p>
  <p class="muted small">Last updated 13 October 2026.</p>
</article>
